+# Automation reliability — Phase 1 review
+
+Base: `424c4920006ab981bbc19f7a7576a1f9ba944d07`
+Branch: `codex/automation-reliability-v1`
+
+Review draft only. No production migration, merge, deployment, scheduled task
+change, enqueue invocation, or prediction generation has been performed.
+Existing prediction/API/HUB files, prediction logic, RANK/TOP5/LAB EYE/LOCAL_MAIN, saved FROZEN
+predictions, HUB design, and hub2-api are unchanged.
+
+## Added files
+
+- `supabase/migrations/20261001131000_automation_reliability_v1.sql`
+- `tests/fixtures/automation-schema.sql`
+- `tests/automation-queue.test.mjs`
+- This document.
+
+The existing schema was inspected using an information_schema SELECT inside a
+read-only transaction. No existing official tables are altered or written by
+the migration or its functions. `post_time` is timestamptz; identity columns
+are date/text/integer/text. PostgreSQL 15+ is required for security-invoker views.
+
+## DB and ownership
+
+`lab_prediction_jobs`: unique race_date/track/race_no/circuit, region,
+QUEUED/CLAIMED/DONE/RETRY/DEAD, attempts, last_error, claimed_by/claimed_at,
+lease_until, next_attempt_at, created_at/updated_at. Additional columns:
+uuid id, claim_token, worker_run_id, max_attempts (default 5, allowed 1–100). Only LOCAL is accepted. Track/region
+consistency and complete claim metadata are enforced with CHECK constraints.
+`updated_at` is maintained by a trigger on the new job table only.
+
+`lab_worker_runs`: uuid id, worker_id, region (four regions or RESCUE),
+started_at/finished_at, claimed/completed/retry/failed counts, last_error,
+RUNNING/SUCCEEDED/FAILED/ABANDONED. Counts are updated transactionally with
+claims and job finishes. A successful run cannot have unresolved/lost claims.
+Lease reclamation increments the new run's claimed_count; the old run retains
+its unresolved count and should be finished as FAILED or ABANDONED.
+There is no automatic abandoned-run cleanup or scheduler in Phase 1.
+
+Tables have RLS enabled, without browser policies. Tables, views, and RPCs are
+available only to service_role (and DB administrators); PUBLIC/anon/authenticated
+access is explicitly revoked. All functions are SECURITY INVOKER with fixed
+search_path; all views use security_invoker=true. service_role is a trusted
+backend credential and must never be exposed in the HUB.
+
+## Mapping
+
+| Region | Tracks |
+| --- | --- |
+| 北海道東北 | 門別、帯広、盛岡、水沢 |
+| 関東 | 浦和、船橋、大井、川崎 |
+| 中部 | 金沢、笠松、名古屋 |
+| 西日本 | 園田、姫路、高知、佐賀 |
+
+Unknown tracks return NULL, are not enqueued, and are counted in health.
+
+## Queue lifecycle
+
+These calls are examples for a future **disposable/staging** environment only.
+They have not been invoked on production.
+
+1. `lab_enqueue_prediction_jobs(race_date)` explicitly populates eligible jobs.
+   Repeated/concurrent inserts use ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING; DONE/DEAD/RETRY are
+   never reset by enqueue. No trigger on official_races and no cron is installed.
+2. `lab_start_worker_run(worker_id, region)` returns the run UUID.
+3. `lab_claim_prediction_jobs(run_id, limit := 1, lease_seconds := 300)`
+   obtains region/identity from the run and atomically returns claimed jobs.
+   Limits: batch 1–50, lease 10–900 seconds. Claim count and attempts increment.
+4. `lab_finish_prediction_job(run_id, job_id, claim_token, outcome, error,
+   retry_seconds := 60, max_attempts := NULL)` accepts DONE/RETRY/DEAD.
+   RETRY sets next_attempt_at; exhaustion becomes DEAD using the job's
+   max_attempts. An optional RPC max_attempts can lower, but never raise, that cap.
+   DONE requires an already saved official prediction with status FROZEN;
+   this function does not generate or save that prediction.
+5. `lab_finish_worker_run(run_id, status := 'SUCCEEDED', error := NULL)`
+   records the finish. Live claims must finish first. Expired/lost claims require
+   FAILED/ABANDONED. Finishing a run does not revoke another run's claim.
+
+Claim uses **FOR UPDATE OF j SKIP LOCKED** in a single transaction. Independent
+workers skip locked job rows; committed live leases are also excluded.
+Only LOCAL, registry PENDING/RETRY, no official prediction of any status sharing the production 3-column identity,
+no legacy saved prediction, future non-NULL post_time, due next_attempt_at,
+and matching region are eligible. Ordering: closest post_time, then stable race
+identity. Normal region workers claim only 60–150 minutes before post_time (inclusive).
+
+RESCUE is a run with region RESCUE. It ignores region filtering but preserves
+all other safety conditions and restricts post_time to 3–70 minutes from now.
+It claims existing queued jobs; it does not implicitly enqueue missing jobs.
+
+An expired CLAIMED job is directly reclaimable while attempts < max_attempts.
+Its attempt count increases and its token is replaced. At the cap, claim RPCs
+retire expired CLAIMED or exhausted QUEUED/RETRY jobs as DEAD before selecting
+work. Cleanup uses SKIP LOCKED and the run's region (all regions for RESCUE),
+independently of post_time/window/registry eligibility. Live last-attempt leases
+are preserved so they can finish. DEAD cleanup clears ownership without counting
+a new claim or attributing a failure to the cleanup run. Old runs keep unresolved
+counts and must be closed as FAILED/ABANDONED. No automatic reaper is installed.
+Job max_attempts and its default can be configured in a future staging/release
+change; raising the cap does not automatically revive DEAD jobs. Finish checks run,
+worker, token, CLAIMED status, and current unexpired lease under row locks.
+An old worker, including one reusing the same worker_id, cannot finish/retry a
+new claim. Errors roll back both queue and run-counter changes.
+
+## Health
+
+Read `lab_prediction_health_today` for the JST race date:
+LOCAL total, FROZEN, QUEUED, CLAIMED, RETRY, DEAD, expired CLAIMED, missing
+prediction within 70 minutes, URGENT_MISSING_PREDICTION within 45 minutes,
+unmapped tracks, and unknown post_time. Empty days return one row with zeros.
+
+Read `lab_prediction_health_races` for race-level reasons and job metadata:
+
+```sql
+SELECT * FROM public.lab_prediction_health_today;
+SELECT race_date, track, race_no, region, post_time, job_status, alert
+FROM public.lab_prediction_health_races
+WHERE race_date = (statement_timestamp() AT TIME ZONE 'Asia/Tokyo')::date
+  AND alert = 'URGENT_MISSING_PREDICTION'
+ORDER BY post_time;
+```
+
+Health includes unqueued races and non-claimable registry statuses. Missing
+means no official or legacy saved prediction; started races are not urgent.
+FROZEN means registry FROZEN, official status FROZEN, or legacy saved output.
+A FROZEN registry with no saved prediction can therefore also raise a missing
+alert, surfacing the inconsistency. Queue counts and FROZEN are independent
+and may overlap when a prediction was saved externally after enqueue.
+Unknown post_time cannot be evaluated against deadlines.
+
+## Validation and remaining release gates
+
+- Existing prediction/API/HUB tests: **54 passed, 0 failed**.
+- New PostgreSQL integration suite: **40 cases authored; 40 skipped** (26 retained + 14 review regressions) because
+  this workspace has no PostgreSQL/psql and no package acquisition was attempted in this revision. SQL syntax/application, two-connection locking, RLS/permissions,
+  and real claim/lease behavior are **not verified**. These are release gates.
+- The test module passes Node syntax validation. It contains no queue mock.
+- Migration filename uses the standard timestamp format, but Supabase CLI
+  generation/listing/advisors could not run because the CLI is unavailable.
+- Protected existing text files match their base Git blob hashes. Binary assets
+  were not downloaded locally because Git transport was unavailable; their
+  original Git tree entries are retained and marked skip-worktree locally.
+
+Integration tests require a freshly initialized, disposable PostgreSQL 15+
+cluster, with no existing anon/authenticated/service_role roles. They create a
+uniquely named empty DB through a local Unix socket; they refuse remote URLs.
+They retain the scratch DB for inspection. Run on a separate local test cluster:
+
+```sh
+LAB_QUEUE_TEST_DISPOSABLE=YES LAB_QUEUE_TEST_SOCKET=/tmp/lab-queue-pg \
+  LAB_QUEUE_TEST_PORT=55432 LAB_QUEUE_TEST_USER=postgres \
+  node tests/automation-queue.test.mjs
+node tests/reliability.test.mjs
+```
+
+The original 26 integration cases include open concurrent transactions, regional scope,
+RESCUE coverage/window, expired/live leases, registry/official/legacy FROZEN,
+started/unknown-time races, retry/backoff, all track mappings, urgency,
+uniqueness/enqueue idempotency, ordering, JRA exclusion, stale token fencing,
+retry exhaustion, DONE guard/payload preservation, run audit, abandoned runs,
+health state counts, status filtering, input validation, and access controls.
+
+Remaining risks:
+
+- Claim checks existing prediction state at statement snapshot time. External
+  writers and existing scheduled tasks do not use this new queue. They can save
+  after a claim; Phase 2 must enforce the current token, lease, pre-race deadline,
+  and saved-prediction uniqueness in its save transaction. Queue RPC fencing
+  alone does not fence writes to official_predictions.
+- Explicit RETRY and expired-lease reclaim share the per-job max_attempts cap.
+  Exhaustion cleanup runs when a claim RPC is invoked for that region (or RESCUE).
+  Without a future caller/reaper, expired exhausted jobs stay visible as expired
+  CLAIMED until that invocation; they cannot be re-claimed past the cap.
+- Post times and registry statuses must remain accurate. No race-registry
+  synchronization or auto-enqueue is introduced in this phase.
+- No full production schema replay or SQL performance plan has been tested.
+  Existing race/prediction identity indexes should be verified in staging.
+- Service-role holders can directly change queue tables; the RPC ownership
+  checks protect cooperating workers, not a malicious backend credential.
+
+Stop here for review. No production application is authorized by this document.
+
